## 1. Count-floor credit for authorized test deletions

ASG executability/runtime_tests.py authorized_count_credits, shared by gate evaluation and checkpoint writing, under-credited authorized test deletions against count_at_least floors measured in executed MTP cases. At step 0013 it credited only 'row'-granularity suites, so deleting one [<Fact>] from a 'method' suite left the floor at 737 against a correct 736. The fix for that (ASG-ERRORS.md:52) credited one unit per deleted method and knowingly left theories under-credited ('fails closed'), with no multi-row test. Step 0059 then escalated on exactly that gap: four theory methods deleted seven cases, 794 vs 797. Under executability profile 1 the older escapes (BASELINE-WAIVED, allow_lower) were disabled, so each occurrence was a deterministic arc blocker. Resolution pattern: the operator explicitly chose an ASG repair plus a normal relaunch without --accept-current-slice each time (.manual/017, .manual/006). Step 0059 also needed an operator arithmetic ruling for 0151/0152/0260 and a recovery of the step-57 case census from the archived TRX. Both were gate-verified after relaunch (checkpoints 736 at idx 12, and 0059's floor).

Severity: high. Categories: asg-tool.
Grouped because: Both incidents share one function and one mechanism: the authorized-delete credit is computed in a unit (methods) that differs from the unit the floor counts (cases). 0059 is a recurrence after an incomplete fix of 0013, not an independent defect. The 0013 fix deliberately deferred the theory case, and the primary report for 0013 had already listed step 59 among the pending steps that would fail.

