### Prevention

- **Compile-time floor simulation: for every count_at_least gate, run the runtime's own authorized_count_credits over the compiled steps. Raise a blocking finding when a step's authorized deletes would earn less credit than the census reduction its acceptance implies. Flag only a net-negative step whose credit is zero or short; never guess the number of theory cases.** (shared; all applicable agents). The defect was visible from compiled descriptors alone: the 0013 report enumerated steps 13, 57, 59, 151, 152 and 157-160. The arc would have stopped at BOOT, before worker tokens were spent, for both the original defect and the theory residue. It is a deterministic pure pass with no retry. Cost: Milliseconds per compile, plus keeping one shared credit function.. Risks/tradeoffs: Theory case counts are unknown before the first measured checkpoint, so the check may false-positive on theory deletes. Mitigate by reading the prior checkpoint's per-method case evidence when it exists. Agent-neutral.. Verification: Fixture spec with a 'method' suite: a single-fact delete, a multi-row theory delete, a 'row' suite and a 'class' suite. Each must produce the expected finding or credit under the pre-fix and post-fix functions..
- **Any count-credit fix must ship with a regression matrix over every granularity it claims to cover: fact, multi-row theory, row suite, class suite and founded suite. Per-method case counts are persisted with each checkpoint, so later credits never depend on archived TRX files.** (shared; all applicable agents). The 0013 fix shipped with a documented under-credit and no theory test. A required matrix would have exposed the 0059 residue at fix time, not 46 steps later. Cost: A handful of unit tests, and a small per-checkpoint JSON growth.. Risks/tradeoffs: None material. Persisting case evidence makes checkpoints larger.. Verification: ASG tests/executability/test_count_credits.py and test_case_counts.py extended to the full matrix. Replay the 0059 case: 4 methods and 7 cases must credit 7..
- **Classify a whole-suite count-floor failure that has zero failures and skips, an exact accepted census and only authorized identities removed as a tool-accounting incident. Escalate it directly instead of spending a generic worker gate-failure retry.** (shared; all applicable agents). At 0059 a worker retry re-ran a deterministic accounting failure that no edit could change (log 3646-3650) before the judge escalated. Cost: One classification predicate in the gate-failure router.. Risks/tradeoffs: Misclassification could skip a retry that a real test loss deserved. The predicate requires an exact census match and zero failures, so a lost test still takes the normal path.. Verification: Replay the 0059 log state. Expect immediate escalation with a tool-accounting label and no worker spawn..

