## 6. End-to-end acceptance with test-only authority hits product defects

Steps 0427, 0428 and 0436 added the AT-1/AT-2 acceptance facts with edit authority confined to test and reference files. Each fact exposed a latent product defect or a false spec premise that only an out-of-scope product change could resolve. At 0427 StagedStudy.engineWith (from 0386/0390) routed QZ-then-LR series paths to fitNonlinear, which refuses anchored gains. A second latent defect (compound analyzer light order) needed a further ruling, .manual/031. At 0428 freshId called Guid.NewGuid directly, so the byte-exact committed-kit fact could never reproduce. At 0436 the 1800 s deadline rested on a sibling harness's 3-minute figure, while the product fit was dominated by a recomputed Jacobian, rhoT allocation and workstation GC. Agents stopped within authority each time. The operator explicitly issued binding rulings (R0001-R0005 in .manual/030, 031, 033, 035, 036) that widened scope to product files. All shipped as operator commits, were gate-verified on normal resume, and later kit-acceptance runs stayed under 3600 s. At 0436 the operator's commit broke elevation (ELEV003/ELEV008 static-let memo), and the resumed worker fixed it.

Severity: medium. Categories: implementation, spec.
Grouped because: The same mechanism: an end-to-end acceptance obligation was planned as a test-only step on the assumption that the product path already met it, and neither the plan nor earlier steps exercised that path through the real dispatch. Three independent product defects, one planning pattern.

