### Prevention

- **At arc boot, record an ASG source stamp: the git HEAD plus the bound-file hash that input_fingerprint already computes. Re-check it cheaply before each gate and before each spawn, and stop immediately with a message naming the changed files.** (shared; all applicable agents). The 0494 change would have been caught within one gate (minutes) instead of after the full verify. 0319 would have been named precisely. Cost: One hash per gate, in milliseconds.. Risks/tradeoffs: None. Agent-neutral.. Verification: During a test arc, modify a validator file between two gates. Expect a stop before the next gate, naming the file..
- **Process: freeze ASG for the duration of an arc, so updates happen only between runs. A boot warning records the HEAD. A relaunch after a tool-drift stop records its decision in .manual. If --accept-current-slice is chosen against the review, the reply states why and what evidence it rests on.** (process; all applicable agents). The trigger was an operator pull, twice (0319, 0494). The undocumented override leaves 0494's acceptance unaudited. Cost: Operator discipline only.. Risks/tradeoffs: It delays urgent tool fixes until a stop. An explicit stop-update-relaunch path remains available.. Verification: Audit the next arc: no ASG reflog entry falls between BOOT and COMPLETE except at recorded stops..

